    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7437" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centŭplex</span></b>  (in MSS. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centĭplex</span></b> ),
			plĭcis, adj.
		centum-plico, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a hundredfold</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 4, 4, 11</span></i>
			 (where Fleck. Krit. Misc. p. 36, would read centupulus; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centuplus): fructus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 7, 220</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centuplicem ferre frugem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. Hist. Sacr. 2, 799</span></i>
			.</div>
